### =============================
### Payment Service API Tests
### =============================
### Prerequisite: payment-service must be running on port 8084.
### Run these requests sequentially from top to bottom.

### 1. Calculate fare for a ride
POST http://localhost:8084/api/payments/calculate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rideId": "ride-123",
  "riderId": "rider-123",
  "driverId": "driver-123",
  "distance": 8.5
}

> {%
    client.test("Fare calculated successfully", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK");
        client.assert(response.body.amount === 177.5, "Amount should match base fare + distance rate");
    });
%}

###

### 2. Get payment by id (replace with a real payment id once one exists)
GET http://localhost:8084/api/payments/000000000000000000000000

> {%
    client.test("Missing payment returns 404", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 404, "Expected 404 Not Found");
    });
%}

###

### 3. Get payment by ride id (replace with a real ride id once one exists)
GET http://localhost:8084/api/payments/ride/ride-123

> {%
    client.test("Missing payment by ride returns 404", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 404, "Expected 404 Not Found");
    });
%}

###

### 4. Get payments by rider id (replace with a real rider id once one exists)
GET http://localhost:8084/api/payments/rider/rider-123

> {%
    client.test("Rider payment history returned", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK");
        client.assert(Array.isArray(response.body), "Response should be a list");
    });
%}

###

### 5. Get payments by driver id (replace with a real driver id once one exists)
GET http://localhost:8084/api/payments/driver/driver-123

> {%
    client.test("Driver earnings history returned", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK");
        client.assert(Array.isArray(response.body), "Response should be a list");
    });
%}